## The Men's Grade Floor — What GIA Standards Say for 1ct

[GIA](https://www.gia.edu/diamond-quality-factor) grades every natural diamond on the 4Cs. For a men's 1ct ring, the grade floor differs from women's. Men's settings are wider and more structural. They don't magnify inclusions the way a prong-heavy halo does.

But 1ct is the size where inclusions can become visible in direct light. The floor matters.

**Color:** G or better. H works in yellow gold where the metal masks color. In white gold or platinum, H reads slightly warm at 1ct. G is the safe entry in any metal.

**Clarity:** VS2 minimum. At 1ct, a [round brilliant cut](/round-cut-diamond) hides inclusions better than any step cut. But an SI1 that is truly eye-clean at this weight is rare in practice. VS2 adds roughly $200 over SI1. That is correct money spent — you are past the threshold where it matters.

**Cut:** Excellent only. Avoid Very Good at 1ct. The fire and brightness difference is visible side by side. GIA Excellent cut costs the same as Very Good in most inventory — there is no good reason to compromise.

| Grade | Natural 1ct Round | What this means |
|---|---|---|
| G-VS2 | [$3,230](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090690?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | The correct entry. Eye-clean, no color in white or yellow gold. |
| G-VS1 | [$3,300](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29161966?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $70 more for one clarity step. Marginal gain at 1ct round. |
| F-VS2 | [$3,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28215109?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $260 premium over G-VS2 for color most buyers cannot see. |
| G-VVS2 | [$3,650](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25530212?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $420 more than entry for clarity no one sees. Skip. |
| E-VS2 | [$3,540](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27878143?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Overkill on color at this carat. Spend the difference on the setting. |
| D-VS2 | [$3,790](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29255579?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $560 premium over G-VS2. D at 1ct in a men's setting is wasted. |

**Verdict:** G-VS2 at $3,230 is the benchmark. Every grade above it costs more without a visible return in a men's setting at this carat weight. Spend the saved money on the setting width and metal quality. For a full breakdown of how GIA grades compare, see our [men's round diamond ring guide](/mens-round-diamond-ring).

