### Setting Type 4 — Geometric / Alternative Metal (Boldest Statement)

Geometric settings wrap the center stone in a shaped frame. Think hexagonal bezels, angular channel walls, or structured cutouts. The stone sits inside the geometry, not on top of it. Alternative metals — tantalum, black titanium — add scratch resistance and a finish white gold cannot replicate.

> "I had a client last month — works construction, hands on tools 10 hours a day. He wanted a 1ct diamond ring he wouldn't have to take off. We went tantalum channel with a bezel-set center. Three months later, the ring looks the same as day one. No scratches, no rhodium wear, nothing. For a man who actually works with his hands, the metal choice matters more than the diamond grade."
> — Farzana Hasan, diamond expert | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

| Ring # | Setting | Metal | Setting Price | Stone | Stone Price | Total | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
