## Expert Summary

Farzana Hasan, [diamond expert](/about-farzana/) at DiamondCritics, has evaluated hundreds of [men's diamond rings](/mens-diamond-rings) across setting types and carat weights.

The men's 1 carat diamond ring decision splits cleanly into two paths. Path one: buy a channel-set band with built-in diamonds for $816–$3,000 and wear it today. Path two: pair a solitaire setting ($1,000–$2,180) with a GIA-certified 1ct natural round from $3,230. Total: $4,230–$5,830.

The correct stone grade for men's settings is G-VS2 Excellent cut. Everything above that grade costs more without a visible return at this carat weight in this setting type.

The critical decision most buyers skip is band width. A 1ct round is 6.4mm across. The band must be at least 5mm to frame it correctly. Confirm width before buying any solitaire setting.

> "Every man who comes in asking about a 1ct ring is really asking two different questions. One is 'can I afford this stone?' The other is 'what will this look like on my hand?' The stone question is answered by the GIA report and the price. The 'look on my hand' question is answered by the setting width and the setting type. I always answer the second question first. The stone can be chosen in 10 minutes once the setting is right."
> — Farzana Hasan, diamond expert | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

